# Template sync record
# Deliberate differences from the template remote; the PR records each audit.
# Derive the baseline for every path from blob equality in template/main history.
# A file matching no historical blob is adapted or project-owned, not a stale copy.
# Read upstream commits for matched copies and every diff hunk for adapted ones.
# This record is not a version pin and does not replace that comparison.

project-owned:
  README.md, Makefile, .gitignore, .github/CODEOWNERS, .github/dependabot.yml,
    .github/workflows/ and docs/architecture/ hold this project's content.
    The template's placeholder CI, ownership and architecture indices cannot
    replace it. check-contents-list.sh belongs to the template's checks;
    this project has its own entry points.

selection:
  All stack-neutral conventions are kept. Go and container images are the
    applicable stack files. FastAPI, NestJS, Next.js and Tailwind are absent.
  No derived stack is selected, so the Extends column and inheritance rules
    remain absent. Revisit if a derived stack is introduced (#684). Template
    af855c1 names that column in §Independence and is not taken with it.
  docs/architecture/structures/ supplies alternatives for a structural choice,
    not additional project rules. The domain shape was chosen in #939 and
    recorded as ADR 0023, with its rules in docs/architecture/structure.md;
    the folder itself is not copied, as the template's architecture index
    directs once the choice has landed.

deliberate-differences:
  AGENTS.md keeps host-defined PM/worker/QA roles, the dev/main rule, secret
    custody and conversation-language requirements. The template's role
    definitions and template-wide rule-admission policy do not replace them.
  git.md keeps tasks based on dev, batch promotion to main (#753), and the
    host-namespace prefix interpretation (#623). The author-preservation
    obligation is adapted to task squash merges into dev. The promotion
    merge method is the template's (ddfa4fb); who opens a promotion stays
    in §Branches, which the template does not state, and the §Commits
    sentence on titles reaching main is dropped because §PRs states it.
  documentation.md owns claim evidence and negative-result methods for documents
    and GitHub artifacts, including reviews (#746); review.md keeps review procedure
    without repeating those general rules.
  documentation.md keeps its build/configuration prose scope (#454), the
    issue-completeness rule (#648), and wording about projects beyond this
    one rather than projects consuming this template.
  ci.md keeps the project's prose entry-point description, release separation,
    hooks and same-tag digest-refresh requirement. It does not import a
    placeholder Makefile. The selection-reporting addition in template
    cccfb36 is deferred: current targets print counts without that selection
    description, so adopting it needs a change to the entry points too.
  review.md keeps the reviewed SHA, conditional local
    substitution and its retirement condition, expanded head-check explanation,
    and the two project-specific Verification examples (#623, #663).
  .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md keeps the no-empty-fields instruction,
    consultation evidence and the instruction to surface unnamed cases.
    The whole-check entry point and Restructure rejected fields are adopted.
  stack-go.md remains adapted: hand-written test doubles (#623) and project
    verification details. Upstream 37be164 removed the mandatory
    interface-named package that this project declined (#685); that old
    objection no longer describes upstream. b29f0f1's heading for
    Generated mocks has no counterpart in this project's Test doubles
    section, and §Module / package boundary drops the template's `mocks/`
    bullet for the same reason (#623).
    §Directory layout is the template's as of 6f3ddf8, its Service and
    Library layouts and §Project envelope's composition-site exception
    included, and §Module / package boundary's declare/depend and "The
    import goes one way" bullets and §Error handling's adapter example
    are taken with it (#1030). The Layout A/B/C text deferred before it
    is gone; packages.md, structure.md, the architecture index and ADR
    0001 were updated in the same change.
  .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md's Summary comment keeps "Reference the
    task or issue if one exists", which 7b274c6 replaced with the
    Closes-keyword instruction. .github/ is the PM's, so #1022 does not
    change it.
  docs/architecture/README.md and adr/0000-template.md retain living records
    and continuous numbering. Upstream freezes ADR bodies and adds errata and
    supersession. That changes the project's decision-history policy, so it is
    not adopted as a template wording correction.
    The architecture rules "Structural rules live in `structure.md`", "A
    point the structural rules leave to the project is settled in an ADR"
    and "Structural rules yield only to what a framework imposes" are
    adopted with that difference: upstream, "Structural rules live in
    `structure.md`" keeps structural rules out of the ADR because its body
    is frozen; here the reason is that current state lives in
    responsibility documents ("Decisions land in pairs"), and "A point the
    structural rules leave to the project" lands a settled point as
    "Decisions land in pairs" pairs it.
    §Rules every shape carries (548895a, 133b60c) is bootstrap input: its
    bullets are in structure.md beside the domain shape's rules, and the
    section is declined so the rule is held once and "Structural rules live
    in `structure.md`" stays true.
    Template 1557dd2 and 392fb81 change only that section's opening
    paragraph, so they are declined with it (#1029).

removal-audit:
  Syncs carried forward what the template changed, never what it removed
    (#1022). Until the sync procedure gains a provenance step, every sync
    runs this check by hand on each file that matches no template blob:
    take as baseline the template revision with the smallest diff to the
    copy, then search every template revision for each sentence the copy
    holds and template/main lacks, joining wrapped lines first so a
    sentence split across lines is found. Each sentence found is deleted
    or recorded above with its reason.
  #1022 ran it against template b8b0890 and deleted two stack-go.md
    sentences: §Module / package boundary's "The implementation lives with
    the interface it satisfies" (removed upstream by 0440057) and §Error
    handling's "Domain sentinels in `<domain>.go`" (removed by 2f5871e;
    §Directory layout states the placement).
  #1029 ran it against template a743468. It found only lines recorded
    above, and took the rewrites that had been waiting: 2757013 in
    stack-go.md, and b8b0890, 33c0f43 and 4bcd785 in documentation.md.
  #1034 ran it against template 6f3ddf8. It found only lines recorded
    above, and took 6c60405 and 6f3ddf8 whole.
  #1030 ran it on stack-go.md against template 6f3ddf8 after taking
    §Directory layout. It found no sentence and no line the template
    has removed; the same check on the copy before the change found 32
    sentences and 60 lines, all of them the deferred layout text.
